    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>(18th Level)</em></p><p><em>“Canonically resolved.”</em></p><p>Once per campaign arc, you may declare an event:</p><blockquote><p><strong>Canonically Resolved.</strong></p></blockquote><p>The event:</p><ul><li><p>Cannot generate further cascading consequences</p></li><li><p>Cannot be resurrected, reframed, or re-litigated</p></li><li><p>Cannot be used as leverage in future arcs</p></li></ul><p>You do not undo what happened.<br />You end its narrative propagation.</p><h3>Cost</h3><p>One use per arc. No Surge required.</p><h3>Pushback</h3><p>Using this prematurely or to avoid earned fallout may spike Noise dramatically. Canon does not like being sealed before its time.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
